'''Poultrio''' (トリニティ, ''Toriniti'') is a [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]]/[[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] variant of [[R.Ost]] that appears in the [[:Category:Advent Stages#Great Advent Stages|Great Advent Stage]] [[Invasion of Poultrio]]. They were added in [[Version 15.2 Update|Version 15.2]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Poultrio
|image = E 769.png
|appearance = [[Invasion of Poultrio]]
|money drop = 4,320¢ - 17,064¢
}}

==Enemy==
This unholy trinity has an enormous amount of health, delivers a nonstop flurry of attacks with enough piercing range to hit most midrangers, and boasts blistering speed that allows it to instantly close the distance to the frontline, albeit with slightly lower DPS than most late-game R.Ost variants along with a whopping 20 knockbacks. While its three traits and lack of immunities give it a plethora of weaknesses to exploit, they also grant it three dangerous abilities: a 30% chance to [[Knockback]] units that can weather its blows, a 15% chance to create an [[Explosion]] expanding its area of effect, and a somewhat weak [[Shield]] that fully regenerates on every knockback to significantly resist both raw damage and debuffs. In addition, should it manage to close the distance to the [[Cat Base]], its [[Base Destroyer]] ability will make short work of it.

==Strategy==
[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] is almost mandatory to tackle this feathered fiend, as a combination of Slow, Curse, and Strong vs. Aku allow him to weather its blows and keep it from pushing with either its speed or Knockback, though he will need assistance to consistently break its Shield. [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Newtone]] is a good choice for sub-DPS as his 600 range allows him to outrange Poultrio's Explosion, while also being able to inflict Slow and reposition in a pinch.

Despite a wide range of meatshields resisting at least one of Poultrio's three types on paper, its overwhelming pushing power and Knockback renders conventional meatshielding much less effective. Cats with extremely high effective HP and stamina, cats with [[Dodge]], and [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] can halt its advance, with a talented [[Bondage Cat (Special Cat)|Ultimate Bondage Cat]] being one of the most effective meatshields against it, owing to having a combination of Strong and Dodge vs. Red while being able to momentarily freeze Poultrio when its Shield is down. If one has them, [[Li'l Gau (Rare Cat)|Crystal Li'l Gau Gau]] can resist both the boss' attacks and Knockback, albeit being somewhat slow.

Due to its multiple weaknesses and lack of immunities, status effects can be useful provided their users have enough range or durability to successfully debuff Poultrio while its Shield is down. In particular, it is possible, albeit difficult, to trap Poultrio in a permanent [[Freeze]] loop using units such as [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] or [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]]. This usually involves breaking the boss' Shield and hitting it from outside its range with an initial Freeze (ie. the [[Thunderbolt]] cannon), then piling as many Freeze units on it as possible during the opening. This is a risky strategy that also requires either a constant stream of DPS or Shield Piercers to constantly break its regenerating Shield and allow Freezes to connect; this ends up somehow being the one niche use-case for [[Li'l Cow Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Lion Cat's]] shield piercing talent, since it's one of the few spammable shield piercers.

