==Trivia==
*Poultrio's name is a portmanteau of ''poultry'' and ''trio''.
*Poultrio's Japanese name, トリニティ ''Toriniti'', is a pun on 鳥 ''tori'' (bird) and ''trinity''.
*Poultrio's Japanese description plays off of how 鳥 ''tori'' (bird) sounds similar to トリオ ''torio'' (trio).
*Poultrio being a comedy group may reference the comedy trio [[wikipedia:ja:ダチョウ倶楽部|Dachō Club]] (ダチョウ倶楽部 ''Dachō Kurabu'', "Ostrich Club"), which is also referenced by the Japanese names of [[R.Ost]] and [[Pure Gold R.Ost]].
*With its three heads and [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]]/[[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] typing, Poultrio may represent [https://www.theoi.com/Khthonios/Hekate.html Hecate], a Greek underworld goddess of magic, the Moon, crossroads and the night, represented with three forms, bodies, or heads. She is also associated with dogs, which appear in all stages of [[Invasion of Poultrio]]; one of her familiars is the Trojan Queen [[wikipedia:Hecuba|Hecuba]] transformed into a black dog, which may be referenced by the [[Doge Dark]]s in the [[Feathergeddon I (Merciless)|first]] and [[Feathergeddon: Swan Song (Brutal)|fourth]] stages. Hecate has many epithets, most relevantly Krokopeplos (Κροκόπεπλος, "[[wikipedia:Saffron|saffron]]-cloaked", potentially explaining the Red trait), Nyctipolos (Νυκτιπολος, "night wandering"), Cthonia (Χθωνία, "of the underworld") and Trimorphe (Τρίμορφη, "three-formed"). Its Base Destroyer ability could come from Hecate's father, [[wikipedia:Perses (son of Crius)|Perses]], a Titan god of destruction whose name means "destroyer".
*Since many of the [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Bosses]] appear to have biblical or demonic inspirations, Poultrio's three heads and Aku trait may reference [[wikipedia:Asmodeus|Asmodeus]], a demon from the deuterocanonical [[wikipedia:Book of Tobit|Book of Tobit]] who is associated with the sin of lust. In demonology, Asmodeus has three heads - one of a human, one of a bull and one of a ram - and the leg of a rooster, which may be why Poultrio is named after poultry despite being an ostrich.
**The phrase 爆笑の渦 ''bakushō no uzu'' in Poultrio's Japanese description means "clamor of uproarious laughter", but literally translates to "whirlpool of explosive laughter" or "vortex of explosive laughter". Besides its [[Explosion]] ability, this might allude to the whirlwind in the second circle of Hell (lust) in Dante's ''[[wikipedia:Inferno (Dante)|Inferno]]''.
**Poultrio could also be based on [[wikipedia:Dante's Satan|Dante's Satan]], who has three faces: one red (middle), one a pale yellow (right), and one black (left). Though Poultrio's right head is blue, it does have yellow eyes. Ironically, this triple-faced Satan represents the antithesis of the holy [[wikipedia:Trinity|Trinity]], a word which Poultrio's Japanese name is a pun on.
**Another demon that may have inspired Poultrio is [[wikipedia:Naberius|Naberius]], a Goetic demon who takes the form of a three-headed dog, a raven, or a black crane.
*Poultrio being a three-headed bird could reference:
**[[wikipedia:Trisiras|Trisiras]], an [[wikipedia:Asura|asura]] whose three heads were cut off and became three different birds. In Indian religions, asuras are demon-like beings who oppose the more benevolent gods, the [[wikipedia:Deva (Hinduism)|Devas]], and are associated with many negative emotions and vices such as violence, wrath, pride, envy, and insincerity, although not all asuras are evil.
**The [[wikipedia:Triple-headed eagle|triple-headed eagle]] in multiple heraldries and [[wikipedia:2 Esdras|2 Esdras]], an apocryphal book of the Old Testament.
**The [[wikipedia:Ellén Trechend|Ellén Trechend]] from Irish mythology, a three-headed monster whose species is unknown, but frequently interpreted as a bird. In P.W. Joyce's ''A Smaller Social History of Ancient Ireland'', a three-headed vulture, likely the Ellén Trechend, commands a flock of copper-red birds.
**[https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Dodrio_(Pok%C3%A9mon) Dodrio], an ostrich-like Pokémon with three heads.
*Both Poultrio and [[Killer Cowbird Cat (Enemy)|Killer Cowbird Cat]], another character added in [[Version 15.2 Update|Version 15.2]], are fusions. Poultrio is three comedians in one, while Killer Cowbird Cat is a combination of a [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Cow Cat]] and [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|Bird Cat]] who collided.
*Unlike R.Ost and his other variants, Poultrio only appears to have one claw on each foot.
*Poultrio is the only R.Ost variant to actually hit multiple times per attack, despite all of the others having animations that imply they should be doing so as well.
*All of the [[:Category:Advent Stages#Great Advent Stages|Great Advent Stage]] rewards released before Poultrio have effects that target its traits. [[Jetpack Cat (Rare Cat)|Jetpack Cat]], [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Maize Cat]] and [[Carpenter Cat (Rare Cat)|Carpenter Cat]] are resistant to it, while [[Bowler Cat (Rare Cat)|Bowler Cat]] can slow it.
*Poultrio is the only Great Advent Boss to not be called a "king" in its Japanese description, stage names, nor [[Media:Eve l 262 nyanko images 54fcHPoxyUtPq64TlOAL.png|event poster]].
*Poultrio is the only Great Advent Boss to have no immunities, though its [[Shield]] makes it immune to crowd-control effects when active.
*Poultrio and [[Dark Emperor Santa]] are the only [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku enemies]] to have more than one trait.
**Coincidentally, they both are also [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red enemies]].

